<template>
  <j-page class="store-page security-page">
    <main>
      <section class="security-hero" aria-labelledby="security-title">
        <span class="eyebrow">Trust &amp; security</span>
        <h1 id="security-title">Know what is signed. Decide whom to trust.</h1>
        <p>NexRun verifies bytes and signatures. The Store layers publisher identity, release policy, build evidence, and operational conformance on top.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="catalog-section" aria-labelledby="levels-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Publisher levels</span>
            <h2 id="levels-title">Three labels with different promises</h2>
          </div>
          <p>The label states who stands behind a package — and which gates it had to pass.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="trust-grid">
          <j-card class="trust-card trust-card--official">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><j-icon name="verified"></j-icon></span>
              <h3>Official</h3>
              <p>Maintained by Nextera and required to pass every declared publishing and conformance gate.</p>
              <span class="trust-card__level">endorsement · nextera-maintained</span>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
          <j-card class="trust-card trust-card--verified">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><j-icon name="workspace_premium"></j-icon></span>
              <h3>Verified publisher</h3>
              <p>Publisher identity is verified and automated gates pass, but Nextera does not maintain the application.</p>
              <span class="trust-card__level">endorsement · identity verified</span>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
          <j-card class="trust-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="icon-tile" aria-hidden="true"><j-icon name="groups"></j-icon></span>
              <h3>Community</h3>
              <p>Content can be cryptographically intact without carrying a Nextera endorsement. Review the signer and evidence explicitly.</p>
              <span class="trust-card__level">endorsement · signature only</span>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="catalog-section security-principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Release policy</span>
            <h2 id="principles-title">What “published” must mean</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <j-list class="principle-list">
          <j-list-item>
            <j-item-section class="step-number">01</j-item-section>
            <j-item-section>
              <j-item-label>Immutable identity</j-item-label>
              <j-item-label>Every installed version resolves to a SHA-256 manifest digest before approval.</j-item-label>
            </j-item-section>
          </j-list-item>
          <j-list-item>
            <j-item-section class="step-number">02</j-item-section>
            <j-item-section>
              <j-item-label>Explicit publisher policy</j-item-label>
              <j-item-label>A valid signature is accepted only when its signer matches a trusted publisher identity.</j-item-label>
            </j-item-section>
          </j-list-item>
          <j-list-item>
            <j-item-section class="step-number">03</j-item-section>
            <j-item-section>
              <j-item-label>Traceable build</j-item-label>
              <j-item-label>Signed provenance connects the release to declared source, tools, providers, and output digest.</j-item-label>
            </j-item-section>
          </j-list-item>
          <j-list-item>
            <j-item-section class="step-number">04</j-item-section>
            <j-item-section>
              <j-item-label>Visible authority</j-item-label>
              <j-item-label>Ports, volumes, secrets, resources, identities, and capabilities are shown before deployment.</j-item-label>
            </j-item-section>
          </j-list-item>
          <j-list-item>
            <j-item-section class="step-number">05</j-item-section>
            <j-item-section>
              <j-item-label>Operational evidence</j-item-label>
              <j-item-label>Stateful official packages require restart, backup, and restore evidence — not only schema validation.</j-item-label>
            </j-item-section>
          </j-list-item>
        </j-list>
      </section>

      <section class="boundary-panel" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Runtime boundary</span>
            <h2 id="boundary-title">The Store never touches your daemon</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="boundary-flow">
          <div class="boundary-node">
            <strong><j-icon name="storefront" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>NexRun Store</strong>
            <p>Public discovery surface. Shows requirements, trust status, and evidence.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="boundary-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <j-icon name="arrow_forward"></j-icon>
            <span>produces</span>
          </div>
          <div class="boundary-node">
            <strong><j-icon name="description" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>Installation plan</strong>
            <p>Declared resources, secrets, volumes, and commands — reviewable before anything runs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="boundary-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
            <j-icon name="arrow_forward"></j-icon>
            <span>verified by</span>
          </div>
          <div class="boundary-node boundary-node--daemon">
            <strong><j-icon name="dns" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>NexRun daemon</strong>
            <p>Performs local verification and deployment through its authenticated runtime boundary.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="boundary-note">
          <j-icon name="gpp_good" aria-hidden="true"></j-icon>
          <span><strong>The public Store never talks directly to a privileged NexRun daemon.</strong> It produces a reviewable installation plan; NexRun performs local verification and deployment on your host.</span>
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </j-page>
</template>
